; Provider-route executable family, 2 of 7 — a reference outside the
; extracted set.
;
; This is the case the whole feature exists for: `u_tim` is a typo for a
; name that only appears inside an opaque string, so no static schema
; could have caught it and no identity-route cross-ref could have either.
; The extracted member set is `{u_time, u_res}` and the reference is
; checked against it exactly like a declared name would be — same
; `not_cross_ref`, same slot path.
;
; The second reference resolves, so the miss is the miss and not the
; whole registry having failed to build.
(use-plugin "lines")

(shader :name main :src "u_time\nu_res")

(bind :uniform u_tim)
(bind :uniform u_res)
